# Downloaded model weights and the release smoke clips — gitignored for the same
# reason the STT bench ignores its own: they dwarf the code and are fetched by
# scripts/download_models.py on demand.
models/

# Recorded fixture audio (Phase 1). Participants' voices; never committed.
#
# The whole directory, not `*.wav`: `getUserMedia` records to webm/opus, so a
# take saved before conversion would not match a wav-only rule and
# `git add benchmarks/speaker-id` would commit people's voices. Ground-truth
# metadata is re-included below, since Phase 4 needs the turn logs tracked while
# the audio stays out.
#
# `fixtures/**` and not `fixtures/`: git refuses to re-include anything under an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so the trailing-slash form would make every negation below
# inert and the turn logs would go untracked without saying so. Excluding the
# directory's CONTENTS instead is what leaves the negations reachable.
fixtures/**
!fixtures/**/
!fixtures/**/*.json
!fixtures/**/*.md
!fixtures/.gitkeep

# Public Vietnamese speaker corpora (Phase 1). Gitignored for size and for
# licence: VoxVietnam is cc-by-nc-4.0 and Vietnam-Celeb states no licence at
# all, so neither may be redistributed through this repo. Both are re-fetchable
# by scripts/fetch_corpora.py, and the trial lists are small enough to re-fetch
# in seconds.
corpora/

# esbuild output for the real SpeechGate, rebuilt on every parity run.
.cache/

# Per-run artifacts. CSVs are the evidence behind the gate decisions and are
# committed deliberately when a gate is recorded; plots and audio are not.
results/**/*.png
results/**/*.wav

# Raw per-comparison rows, as opposed to the summaries beside them.
#
# Same distinction this file already draws for the channel session — the
# aggregate commits, the per-row file does not — applied here for size instead
# of for privacy. A `*-pairs.csv` is one row per trial pair and runs to six
# figures: the three from the M11/M11b controls came to 17.5MB together, against
# 6.6MB for everything `results/` held before them. What a gate is argued from
# is the summary CSV, the `.log` and the measurement report, all of which stay
# tracked; these are the derivation, re-derivable from the corpus and the
# committed script.
#
# Size is the reason this rule has to exist rather than a convention: `git rm`
# does not shrink history, so a pairs file is a permanent cost to every clone
# from the commit that adds it onward.
#
# `results/pairwise-pairs.csv` predates this rule and stays tracked. Untracking
# it would drop it from the tree without reclaiming the history it already sits
# in, so the cost is paid either way and the file is left where readers of the
# model screen expect it.
results/**/*-pairs.csv

# Embedding caches. Derived from the corpus above, rebuilt by
# scripts/build_embedding_cache.py, and every consumer already fails with that
# instruction when one is absent — so committing megabytes of it would buy
# nothing the corpus rule does not already forbid redistributing.
results/**/*.npz

# Production turn-metrics sinks. Unlike the CSVs above these are not corpus
# measurements — they are captured from live sessions, and their rows carry a
# `sessionId` plus `speechStartedAt`/`speechEndedAt` as epoch wall-clock
# (`ws-events.ts:242,244`), not durations. A JSONL under results/ is therefore
# assumed to be production capture until proven otherwise, and stays local.
# Commit a coarsened derivative if a run needs to be reproducible.
results/**/*.jsonl

# Per-turn rows from the browser-channel session, for the same reason one step
# further on. `results/` is tracked, so a per-turn CSV lands in git history — and
# the channel session is recorded from real people under a stated destruction
# date. The aggregate `channel-delta.csv` is nine columns of EERs per model and
# bucket and commits fine; this one is one row per turn somebody actually spoke,
# carrying their pseudonym, where they stood, which language they used and how
# every clip scored.
#
# The failure that guards against is the one Phase 2 already caught in the turn
# log, in a new location: the audio is destroyed on the promised date, the
# retention step is logged as complete, and a per-turn record of the session
# stays in the repository forever. `git rm` does not remove it from history.
results/channel-delta-turns.csv

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
